 "title": "Brown County Ohio Government Portal - Treasurer",
 "text": "Brown County Ohio Government Portal - Treasurer\nHome\nFAQs\nLinks\nTowns & Villages\nNews\nBrown County Treasurer\nTreasurer Traci Stamper\nAddress\nAdministration Building\n800 Mt. Orab Pike\nSuite 171\nGeorgetown, Ohio 45121\nTelephone 937.378.6705 or toll free 800.229.6177\nOffice Hours 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Monday-Friday\nWebsite http://www.TreasurerBrownCounty.com\nEmail T reasurer@BrownCountyOhio.gov\nThe Treasurer is the custodian of all of the county's revenue and assets. The Treasurer's banking function includes serving as the county's chief investment officer. Under strict legal guidelines, the Treasurer invests unspent revenue in interest-bearing commericial funds that generate added revenue for the county.\nReal and personal property taxes are collected by the Treasurer, in addition to estate taxes and taxes on manufactured homes. The Treasurer collects delinquent taxes.\nElected Officials\nAuditor\nClerk of Courts\nCommissioners\nCommon Pleas\nCoroner\nEngineer\nMunicipal Judge\nProbate/Juvenile\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nQuick Information\n∙ Brown-Adams County Resource Guide\n∙ County Map\n∙ Brown County Comprehensive Plan\n∙ Legal Holidays\n∙ School Districts\n∙ Telephone Numbers\n∙ Emergency Info\n∙ Township Officials\nNews & Postings\nContractor Information: Community Housing Impact & Preservation Program (CHIP) Contractor\nAberdeen\nFayetteville\nGeorgetown\nHamersville\nHigginsport\nMount Orab\nRipley\nRussellville\nSardinia\nSaint Martin\nLake Lorelei\nLake Waynoka",
